{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018nkT17bkTJj2Gvq4FFpof9","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→'use client'\n     2→\n     3→import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\n     4→import { formatNumber } from '@/lib/utils'\n     5→\n     6→interface Page {\n     7→  id: string\n     8→  name: string\n     9→  instagram_business_account: {\n    10→    id: string\n    11→  }\n    12→}\n    13→\n    14→interface MediaItem {\n    15→  id: string\n    16→  caption?: string\n    17→  media_type: string\n    18→  media_url?: string\n    19→  thumbnail_url?: string\n    20→  permalink?: string\n    21→  timestamp: string\n    22→  insights?: {\n    23→    reach?: number\n    24→    likes?: number\n    25→    comments?: number\n    26→    shares?: number\n    27→    saves?: number\n    28→  }\n    29→}\n    30→\n    31→export default function DashboardPage() {\n    32→  const [pages, setPages] = useState<Page[]>([])\n    33→  const [selectedPage, setSelectedPage] = useState<Page | null>(null)\n    34→  const [media, setMedia] = useState<MediaItem[]>([])\n    35→  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)\n    36→  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)\n    37→\n    38→  // Fetch user's Facebook pages\n    39→  useEffect(() => {\n    40→    async function fetchPages() {\n    41→      try {\n    42→        const res = await fetch('/api/meta/me')\n    43→        if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch pages')\n    44→        const data = await res.json()\n    45→        setPages(data.pages)\n    46→        if (data.pages.length === 1) {\n    47→          setSelectedPage(data.pages[0])\n    48→        }\n    49→      } catch (err: any) {\n    50→        setError(err.message)\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55793a17-4f50-4b66-a54a-24d9bccc2747","uuid":"2f546fb8-6f6b-458f-968e-44c8a8275007","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/MetaCoach/app/dashboard/page.tsx","content":"'use client'\n\nimport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\nimport { formatNumber } from '@/lib/utils'\n\ninterface Page {\n  id: string\n  name: string\n  instagram_business_account: {\n    id: string\n  }\n}\n\ninterface MediaItem {\n  id: string\n  caption?: string\n  media_type: string\n  media_url?: string\n  thumbnail_url?: string\n  permalink?: string\n  timestamp: string\n  insights?: {\n    reach?: number\n    likes?: number\n    comments?: number\n    shares?: number\n    saves?: number\n  }\n}\n\nexport default function DashboardPage() {\n  const [pages, setPages] = useState<Page[]>([])\n  const [selectedPage, setSelectedPage] = useState<Page | null>(null)\n  const [media, setMedia] = useState<MediaItem[]>([])\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)\n\n  // Fetch user's Facebook pages\n  useEffect(() => {\n    async function fetchPages() {\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch('/api/meta/me')\n        if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch pages')\n        const data = await res.json()\n        setPages(data.pages)\n        if (data.pages.length === 1) {\n          setSelectedPage(data.pages[0])\n        }\n      } catch (err: any) {\n        setError(err.message)","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":240}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Kg1dkhmAbpgLEznzDJMwRi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This appears to be a dashboard for managing pages/media, but the core features specified in the feature list don't match what's currently implemented. The features list is for a Meta Ads coaching platform focused on:\n1. Ad account management\n2. Campaign performance analysis  \n3. Coaching recommendations\n4. Client dashboards and reporting\n\nBut what's implemented seems more geared toward Instagram/Facebook content management.\n\nLet me start with a strategic approach. Since there are 52 features organized in phases, I should:\n\n1. Start with Phase 1: Core Infrastructure & Authentication (highest priority P0 features)\n   - INFRA-001: Supabase Database Schema\n   - AUTH-001, AUTH-002, AUTH-003: Authentication\n   - API-001, API-002: API endpoints\n\n2. The project already has a build that succeeds. Let me create a comprehensive implementation plan by starting with the most critical features.\n\nLet me start by creating the core features systematically. First, I'll create the API health endpoint (API-001) which is the simplest and most critical, then move to infrastructure and auth.\n\nLet me create a comprehensive feature implementation starting with API-001:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":771,"cache_read_input_tokens":104493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":771},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55793a17-4f50-4b66-a54a-24d9bccc2747","uuid":"60885601-ee6c-4a86-be9c-6b46a70c3123"}
